      "math_academy_id": "e-15054",
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X \\sim B(6, 0.67)$ given below, compute $P(X=2).$\n\n| $\\quad x \\quad$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\leq x)$ | $\\,0.0013\\,$ | $\\,0.0170\\,$ | $\\,0.0969\\,$ | $\\,0.3130\\,$ | $\\,0.6422\\,$ | $\\,0.9095\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x) = P(X \\leq x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(X\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1\\})+P(X=2) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =F(1)+P(X=2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2) & =F(2)-F(1) \\\\  & =0.0969-0.0170 \\\\  & =0.0799\\end{aligned}\n$$",
